      "retweet": {
        "id": "2103183639383298066",
        "text": "Gavin Baker owned 15% of Nvidia and 10% of Tesla sub-$2 billion. His biggest regret won't be either. It'll be the price you'll pay for SpaceX after the IPO.\n\n\"A company like this comes once in your career. Thank God I took it. Plenty of people didn't.\"\n\nHis analog: British East India Company. Empire scale, not tech scale.\n\nThe setup:\n\n- 10,000 SpaceX employees could have sold every 6 months for a decade\n- Almost nobody did\n- Secondary pricing is a decade underpriced\n\nBaker on the Elon-Anthropic partnership: \"Four months ago it didn't exist. Then it made sense. Everyone has a price.\"\n\nIncumbents realign around SpaceX gravity when it moves.\n\nThe IPO doesn't price the company. It prices the last window.",
        "created_at": "Thu Sep 24 18:03:49 +0000 2026",
        "lang": "en",
        "media": [
          {
            "type": "video",
            "id": "2103182879022878722",
